  "body": "3D Deburr now sizes a chamfer by its contact chord width or its perpendicular chord depth. The generator calculates the actual cone contacts with both faces. It refuses unsupported contacts and cuts outside the declared size bound.\n\nThe controls add Constant Width, Constant Depth, a break profile, and the number of passes. A Round profile refuses a sharp cone. Every pass must stay inside the tip window. The generator checks every pass before it emits travel.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: The public Deburr `width` parameter changes from cone setback to contact chord width. MCP clients must supply chord width. The project format is v76. The loader converts Deburr widths from older files by `sqrt(2)`. It preserves the v75 machine controller data. The merge commit declares this change with `feat(deburr)!` and a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.\n\nThe independent pins measure the cutter intersections with both faces. They also cover the narrow multi-pass window and migration from a main-written v75 file. Validation details and screenshots follow below.\n\nChangelog: 3D Deburr adds contact chord width and depth sizing, multiple passes, and explicit refusal for unsupported cone contacts or pass windows. Older project widths are converted on load.\n\nEffort: high\n\n\nBefore, original width controls:\n\n![Original Deburr controls](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/12fd8382720801e592c9d365eff7ce9145d0e946/pr-3220/before.png)\n\nAfter, Constant Width with three passes:\n\n![Constant Width controls](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/12fd8382720801e592c9d365eff7ce9145d0e946/pr-3220/after-width.png)\n\nAfter, Constant Depth with three passes:\n\n![Constant Depth controls](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/12fd8382720801e592c9d365eff7ce9145d0e946/pr-3220/after-depth.png)\n\nThese focused captures render the actual egui controls. The images are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch. No capture harness, image, or review log is in this PR branch.\n\nReview-fix pins:\n\n- Pass window: `multiple_passes_refuse_a_window_that_only_contains_the_final_tip`.\n- Safe travel: `clearance_normalizes_the_numeric_skin_before_any_traverse`.\n- Width contacts: `constant_width_measures_actual_cone_contacts_on_120_and_90_degree_wedges`.\n- Depth contacts: `constant_depth_measures_actual_cone_contacts_on_120_and_90_degree_wedges`.\n- Unsupported contacts: `a_real_bottom_face_without_cone_contact_refuses_by_name`.\n- Main v75 migration: `main_v75_deburr_migrates_once_and_preserves_the_machine_controller`.\n- The existing `continuous_4axis_part` suite pins the example version.\n\nTen mutation groups failed at the intended assertions. Each passed after the original source bytes were restored.\n\nThe full quick gate ran all 308 steps. It passed 305 steps. The example version and the window-floor candidate checks caused two failures. The UI library also exited with SIGSEGV during that run. After the two corrections, the failed-step quick gate passed all three steps on the final head. The UI library passed 1,402 tests with seven ignored at the same thread count. The SIGSEGV did not repeat.\n\nPixel snapshots and heavy lanes were not run for this author-side fix.\n\nFinal head: `026a798beca9675c2938bd0cae3d73a99867ccb7`.\n\nThe final affected suites passed: 31 motion tests and 148 app tests, with six app tests ignored.\n\n`cargo clippy -j 8 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\nFixes #1890\n",
